{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-26319","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-30463","text":"RRABBIT"}]},{"id":"blk-26320","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30464","text":"The road as a windowing system — half of "},{"id":"spn-30465","marks":["bold"],"text":"T&R (Travel & RRABBIT)"},{"id":"spn-30466","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-26321","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30467","marks":["bold"],"text":"Travel and RRABBIT are two personalities, not two layers."},{"id":"spn-30468","text":" Travel wants to navigate: the road, the camera, the flight into a window, the districts. RRABBIT wants to "},{"id":"spn-30469","marks":["italic"],"text":"be"},{"id":"spn-30470","text":" the windows — the sign standing on the road, the surface that flattens to 1:1 under you, the rect that decides a click is yours. One likes going; the other likes being gone to."}]},{"id":"blk-26322","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30471","text":"This repo is a fork of "},{"id":"spn-30472","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"../RAVIO"}],"text":"RAVIO"},{"id":"spn-30473","text":"'s world, re-missioned from "},{"id":"spn-30474","marks":["italic"],"text":"rendering a build harness"},{"id":"spn-30475","text":" to "},{"id":"spn-30476","marks":["italic"],"text":"managing an operating system's windows"},{"id":"spn-30477","text":", and it holds both of them — as two modules rather than one file:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-26324","spans":[{"id":"spn-30478","text":"file"}]},{"id":"blk-26325","spans":[{"id":"spn-30479","text":"who"}]},{"id":"blk-26326","spans":[{"id":"spn-30480","text":"what is in it"}]}],"id":"blk-26323","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-26327","spans":[{"id":"spn-30481","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"m2/travel.js"}],"text":"`m2/travel.js`"}]},{"id":"blk-26328","spans":[{"id":"spn-30482","text":"Travel"}]},{"id":"blk-26329","spans":[{"id":"spn-30483","text":"poses, districts, overview, the flatten, the flight, input routing"}]}],[{"id":"blk-26330","spans":[{"id":"spn-30484","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"m2/rrabbit.js"}],"text":"`m2/rrabbit.js`"}]},{"id":"blk-26331","spans":[{"id":"spn-30485","text":"RRABBIT"}]},{"id":"blk-26332","spans":[{"id":"spn-30486","text":"texture adoption, signs, popups, the ledger rect"}]}],[{"id":"blk-26333","spans":[{"id":"spn-30487","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"m2/world.js"}],"text":"`m2/world.js`"}]},{"id":"blk-26334","spans":[{"id":"spn-30488","text":"neither"}]},{"id":"blk-26335","spans":[{"id":"spn-30489","text":"the stage: scene handles, the "},{"id":"spn-30490","marks":["code"],"text":"signs"},{"id":"spn-30491","text":" ledger, the numbers the HUD reads"}]}],[{"id":"blk-26336","spans":[{"id":"spn-30492","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"m2/shell.js"}],"text":"`m2/shell.js`"}]},{"id":"blk-26337","spans":[{"id":"spn-30493","text":"the wiring"}]},{"id":"blk-26338","spans":[{"id":"spn-30494","text":"builds the world, drives the frame, owns the diagnostics"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-26339","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30495","text":"They say very little to each other. Travel reads two things and both come through the shared ledger rather than a call — which sign stands at an address, and what rect it owns in the flat output. RRABBIT calls Travel "},{"id":"spn-30496","marks":["bold"],"text":"once"},{"id":"spn-30497","text":": when a window dies while you are standing in it, it tells Travel to let go. That is the whole conversation, and it runs in one direction."}]},{"id":"blk-26340","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30498","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"https://github.com/c-u-l8er/travel-and-rrabbit"}],"text":"travel-and-rrabbit"},{"id":"spn-30499","text":" is the distribution — it carries Travel's name and is not Travel either."}]},{"id":"blk-26341","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30500","text":"Signs on the road are no longer journal rows. "},{"id":"spn-30501","marks":["bold"],"text":"They are the running applications."},{"id":"spn-30502","text":" The vacuum tubes are no longer lane ratings; they are CPU, RAM, swap, disk, net, temp and load. Districts are no longer amp workspaces; they are desktop workspaces. You drive past your windows, fly into one, and it flattens into a real, square, pixel-exact surface you can type into."}]},{"id":"blk-26342","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30503","text":"It shows only windows launched into it. It does not replace your desktop."}]},{"id":"blk-26343","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30504","marks":["bold"],"text":"Read [`docs/spec/README.md`](docs/spec/README.md) first"},{"id":"spn-30505","text":" — in particular §2, which records what does "},{"id":"spn-30506","marks":["italic"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-30507","text":" work about the obvious integration and why."}]},{"id":"blk-26344","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-30508","text":"Status"}]},{"id":"blk-26345","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30509","marks":["bold"],"text":"M0–M5 built, M0–M4 measured"},{"id":"spn-30510","text":" (2026-08-08), each with measurements rather than screenshots alone — spec §10–§12 and §14–§17. "},{"id":"spn-30511","marks":["bold"],"text":"Booted on T&R 2026-08-09."}]},{"id":"blk-26346","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-26348","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30512","marks":["bold"],"text":"M0"},{"id":"spn-30513","text":" — the road occludes a live Wayland surface. This was the gate."}]}],"id":"blk-26347","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-26350","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30514","marks":["bold"],"text":"M1"},{"id":"spn-30515","text":" — many windows ride the road as signs, one adopted GPU texture each,"}]}],"id":"blk-26349","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-26351","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30516","text":"at stable milepost addresses. No Greenfield patch was needed after all (§11.1)."}]},{"id":"blk-26352","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-26354","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30517","marks":["bold"],"text":"M2"},{"id":"spn-30518","text":" — flying into a sign arrives fronto-parallel at exactly 1:1, where it"}]}],"id":"blk-26353","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-26355","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30519","text":"can be pointed at, typed into, and left with a chord no client can swallow."}]},{"id":"blk-26356","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-26358","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30520","marks":["bold"],"text":"M3"},{"id":"spn-30521","text":" — seven tubes reading the real machine, and a rack that is not allowed"}]}],"id":"blk-26357","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-26359","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30522","text":"to show a number it cannot explain."}]},{"id":"blk-26360","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-26362","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30523","marks":["bold"],"text":"M4"},{"id":"spn-30524","text":" — three districts as workspaces, each a road of its own, and a ledger"}]}],"id":"blk-26361","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-26363","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30525","text":"where every window has its own rect so input resolves by position (§15.2)."}]},{"id":"blk-26364","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-26366","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30526","marks":["bold"],"text":"popups"},{"id":"spn-30527","text":" — §7's open problem, closed (§16). Also found that an "},{"id":"spn-30528","marks":["code"],"text":"xdg_popup"}]}],"id":"blk-26365","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-26367","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30529","text":"cannot map at all in Greenfield rc1."}]},{"id":"blk-26368","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-26370","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30530","marks":["bold"],"text":"M5"},{"id":"spn-30531","text":" — runs as a session: Python-only on the target, and Firefox runs the"}]}],"id":"blk-26369","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-26371","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30532","text":"whole shell."}]},{"id":"blk-26372","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-26374","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30533","marks":["bold"],"text":"BOOT"},{"id":"spn-30534","text":" — "},{"id":"spn-30535","marks":["bold"],"text":"runs on a T&R image"},{"id":"spn-30536","text":" (2026-08-09). Greeter to road on the"}]}],"id":"blk-26373","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-26375","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30537","text":"distribution it is built for, in a 4 GB guest with no GPU. Six of seven tubes read the real FreeBSD machine; "},{"id":"spn-30538","marks":["code"],"text":"temp"},{"id":"spn-30539","text":" reports its own absence, because a VM has no "},{"id":"spn-30540","marks":["code"],"text":"dev.cpu.0.temperature"},{"id":"spn-30541","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-26376","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30542","text":"Three things that only a real boot could have found, all now fixed:"}]},{"id":"blk-26377","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-26379","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30543","marks":["bold"],"text":"`make.sh` could not carry the shell to the builder at all."},{"id":"spn-30544","text":" "},{"id":"spn-30545","marks":["code"],"text":"build-image.sh"}]}],"id":"blk-26378","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-26380","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30546","text":"reads "},{"id":"spn-30547","marks":["code"],"text":"RRABBIT_DIST"},{"id":"spn-30548","text":" as a path on the machine doing the build, and that machine is never the workstation — so there was no route from a built bundle to an image. It pushes "},{"id":"spn-30549","marks":["code"],"text":"dist/"},{"id":"spn-30550","text":" + "},{"id":"spn-30551","marks":["code"],"text":"bridge.py"},{"id":"spn-30552","text":" now, and refuses a "},{"id":"spn-30553","marks":["code"],"text":"dist/"},{"id":"spn-30554","text":" older than its sources."}]},{"id":"blk-26381","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-26383","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30555","marks":["bold"],"text":"The FreeBSD tube reader had never executed."},{"id":"spn-30556","text":" "},{"id":"spn-30557","marks":["code"],"text":"net"},{"id":"spn-30558","text":" raised "},{"id":"spn-30559","marks":["code"],"text":"TypeError"},{"id":"spn-30560","text":" on a"}]}],"id":"blk-26382","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-26384","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30561","marks":["code"],"text":"None"},{"id":"spn-30562","text":" peak the first time it ran. Fixed by giving it the same prior-peak protocol "},{"id":"spn-30563","marks":["code"],"text":"LinuxReader"},{"id":"spn-30564","text":" already had — patching only the crash would have re-introduced the bug that note describes, where the first byte pins the gauge at 100%."}]},{"id":"blk-26385","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-26387","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30565","marks":["bold"],"text":"The greeter preselected RRABBIT, and could not select anything else."},{"id":"spn-30566","text":" Two"}]}],"id":"blk-26386","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-26388","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30567","marks":["code"],"text":".desktop"},{"id":"spn-30568","text":" entries, picked by sort order, and "},{"id":"spn-30569","marks":["code"],"text":"rrabbit"},{"id":"spn-30570","text":" sorts before "},{"id":"spn-30571","marks":["code"],"text":"tandr"},{"id":"spn-30572","text":" — so a fresh image logged into the 3D shell, which is precisely what "},{"id":"spn-30573","marks":["code"],"text":"rrabbit-session"},{"id":"spn-30574","text":" says must never happen. The session label was blank as well: it asked SDDM's "},{"id":"spn-30575","marks":["code"],"text":"SessionModel"},{"id":"spn-30576","text":" for "},{"id":"spn-30577","marks":["code"],"text":"Qt.DisplayRole"},{"id":"spn-30578","text":", which that model does not publish. T&R now seeds the default and the greeter takes "},{"id":"spn-30579","marks":["bold"],"text":"F2"},{"id":"spn-30580","text":" to change it."}]},{"id":"blk-26389","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30581","marks":["bold"],"text":"Native applications work"},{"id":"spn-30582","text":" (§18). A real "},{"id":"spn-30583","marks":["code"],"text":"xterm"},{"id":"spn-30584","text":" runs on the road — X11 → XWayland → nested compositor → h264 → browser → GPU texture → sign — flattened to "},{"id":"spn-30585","marks":["bold"],"text":"960×653 at `scale 1.0000`"},{"id":"spn-30586","text":", prompt legible. §13 spent its whole length searching the environment and the cause was not in the environment: the official addon build "},{"id":"spn-30587","marks":["bold"],"text":"compiles its own GStreamer at branch 1.20"},{"id":"spn-30588","text":" and this machine runs "},{"id":"spn-30589","marks":["bold"],"text":"1.28.6"},{"id":"spn-30590","text":", so the shipped "},{"id":"spn-30591","marks":["code"],"text":"libproxy-encoding.so"},{"id":"spn-30592","text":" linked a GStreamer GL that was not the installed one. Every symbol resolved the entire time it was silently emitting nothing — "},{"id":"spn-30593","marks":["code"],"text":"ldd"},{"id":"spn-30594","text":" resolving is not evidence a native module matches its dependencies. The rebuild is now "},{"id":"spn-30595","marks":["code"],"text":"npm run addons"},{"id":"spn-30596","text":", pinned and hash-checked (§19)."}]},{"id":"blk-26390","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30597","text":"Still true, and not smoothed over:"}]},{"id":"blk-26391","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-26393","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30598","marks":["bold"],"text":"Frames tear — two thirds fixed, and the rest now measured"},{"id":"spn-30599","text":" (§20). It was"}]}],"id":"blk-26392","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-26394","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30600","text":"never a damage-region problem. three left a "},{"id":"spn-30601","marks":["bold"],"text":"vertex array bound"},{"id":"spn-30602","text":" and Greenfield's YUV→RGB pass binds none of its own, so it recorded its attribute pointers into three's VAO and drew with three's leftovers; that was the full-canvas magnified-glyph artifact, and it is gone. Separately the decoded texture is "},{"id":"spn-30603","marks":["bold"],"text":"larger than the surface"},{"id":"spn-30604","text":" — 1024×770 for a 960×653 xterm — and the sign was mapping the padding too; it now samples the same sub-rect Greenfield's own shader does. What remains is a constant-slope diagonal with flat cyan below it, inside the decoded content: chroma left at default, so never written. That is upstream in "},{"id":"spn-30605","marks":["code"],"text":"@gfld/compositor"},{"id":"spn-30606","text":", and the encoder A/B that would narrow it could not be run — see §20.3."}]},{"id":"blk-26395","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-26397","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30607","marks":["bold"],"text":"Per-window encode cost is still unpriced, and §21.2 says why."},{"id":"spn-30608","text":" Two"}]}],"id":"blk-26396","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-26398","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30609","text":"harnesses, neither monotonic in window count. What they did establish: the proxy is flat at ~0.4% CPU while the browser sits at 425%, so the expensive half is decode and composite, not encode — \"per-window encode cost\" may be the wrong first question."}]},{"id":"blk-26399","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-26401","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30610","marks":["bold"],"text":"Native launches drop above two"},{"id":"spn-30611","text":" (§21.3). Ask for four windows, get two,"}]}],"id":"blk-26400","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-26402","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30612","text":"with nothing reported. Found while measuring something else, not diagnosed. The multi-window case is not just unpriced, it is unreliable."}]},{"id":"blk-26403","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-26405","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30613","marks":["bold"],"text":"Signs carry no titles yet."}]}],"id":"blk-26404","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-26406","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30614","text":"Closed since: a "},{"id":"spn-30615","marks":["bold"],"text":"reload no longer strands the remote client"},{"id":"spn-30616","text":" (§21.1) — each page load takes a fresh session id and "},{"id":"spn-30617","marks":["code"],"text":"pagehide"},{"id":"spn-30618","text":" reaps the old one, verified across three reloads against a proxy that was never restarted, leaving exactly one "},{"id":"spn-30619","marks":["code"],"text":"xterm"},{"id":"spn-30620","text":" behind."}]},{"id":"blk-26407","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30621","marks":["code"],"text":"xdg_popup"},{"id":"spn-30622","text":" is no longer on this list — §16 closed it, and found on the way that a popup cannot map at all in Greenfield rc1."}]},{"id":"blk-26408","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-30623","text":"Local patches — do not lose these"}]},{"id":"blk-26409","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30624","text":"RRABBIT carries a "},{"id":"spn-30625","marks":["bold"],"text":"required"},{"id":"spn-30626","text":" one-line fix to "},{"id":"spn-30627","marks":["code"],"text":"@gfld/compositor"},{"id":"spn-30628","text":": without it an "},{"id":"spn-30629","marks":["code"],"text":"xdg_popup"},{"id":"spn-30630","text":" can never map, so "},{"id":"spn-30631","marks":["bold"],"text":"no client can show a menu, dropdown or tooltip"},{"id":"spn-30632","text":". "},{"id":"spn-30633","marks":["code"],"text":"node_modules/"},{"id":"spn-30634","text":" is gitignored, so the fix lives in "},{"id":"spn-30635","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"patches/"}],"text":"`patches/`"},{"id":"spn-30636","text":" and is re-applied by "},{"id":"spn-30637","marks":["code"],"text":"postinstall"},{"id":"spn-30638","text":" and by "},{"id":"spn-30639","marks":["code"],"text":"build"},{"id":"spn-30640","text":". A runtime detector warns if it is ever missing rather than silently repairing it."}]},{"id":"blk-26410","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30641","text":"Read "},{"id":"spn-30642","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"patches/README.md"}],"text":"`patches/README.md`"},{"id":"spn-30643","text":" before touching "},{"id":"spn-30644","marks":["code"],"text":"package.json"},{"id":"spn-30645","text":" scripts or upgrading "},{"id":"spn-30646","marks":["code"],"text":"@gfld/compositor"},{"id":"spn-30647","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-26411","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-30648","text":"Lineage"}]},{"id":"blk-26412","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-26414","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30649","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"../RAVIO"}],"text":"RAVIO"},{"id":"spn-30650","text":" — the world this forks, and the source of every measured"}]}],"id":"blk-26413","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-26415","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30651","text":"constant ("},{"id":"spn-30652","marks":["code"],"text":"S"},{"id":"spn-30653","text":", "},{"id":"spn-30654","marks":["code"],"text":"BOOST_X"},{"id":"spn-30655","text":", "},{"id":"spn-30656","marks":["code"],"text":"MIR_TILT"},{"id":"spn-30657","text":", the hood clip, the yoke camera framing)"}]},{"id":"blk-26416","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-26418","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30658","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"https://github.com/c-u-l8er/PARKVPS"}],"text":"PARKVPS"},{"id":"spn-30659","text":" — the fleet whose rail proved"}]}],"id":"blk-26417","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-26419","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30660","text":"the tab strip shape, and the origin of the "},{"id":"spn-30661","marks":["code"],"text":"Ctrl+Alt+Shift+Esc"},{"id":"spn-30662","text":" escape hatch"}]},{"id":"blk-26420","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-26422","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30663","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"https://github.com/udevbe/greenfield"}],"text":"Greenfield"},{"id":"spn-30664","text":" — the in-browser Wayland"}]}],"id":"blk-26421","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-26423","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30665","text":"compositor, AGPL-3.0"}]},{"id":"blk-26424","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-26426","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30666","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"https://www.collabora.com/news-and-blog/news-and-events/wxrd-a-standalone-wayland-compositor-for-xrdesktop.html"}],"text":"wxrd"}]}],"id":"blk-26425","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-26427","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30667","text":"/ "},{"id":"spn-30668","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"https://github.com/evil0sheep/motorcar"}],"text":"motorcar"},{"id":"spn-30669","text":" — the 3D-windowing prior art, and where the scoping decision comes from"}]},{"id":"blk-26428","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-30670","text":"Licence"}]},{"id":"blk-26429","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-30671","text":"AGPL-3.0, inherited from Greenfield. See spec §9."}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaierafevm6oyr4ssrmdbzbxnyzmkfijzvs5echdavles3tk4outrir44q","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}